.TH BWX 1 "2026-11-07" "bwx 1.3.2" "User Commands"
.\"
.SH NAME
bwx \- Bitwarden Secrets Manager eXtended CLI
.\"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bwx
.I command
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ args... ]
.br
.B bwx
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.br
.B bwx
.BR \-v | \-\-version
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bwx
extends the official Bitwarden Secrets Manager CLI
.RB ( bws )
with operational lifecycle management for secrets.
Features include bulk release tagging, versioned cloning, structured
metadata in secret notes, expiry tracking, and provider-driven credential
rotation.
.PP
Commands are organized into families:
.BR secret ,
.BR project ,
.BR config ,
.BR tag ,
.BR import ,
.BR check ,
.BR note ,
.BR rotate ,
.BR provider ,
.BR raw ,
and
.BR completion .
The dispatch layer accepts up to three positional words to resolve a
subcommand (for example,
.BR "bwx project default id" ).
.PP
.B bwx
requires Bash 4.0 or newer.
macOS ships Bash 3.2; install an updated version via Homebrew or pkgsrc.
.PP
When
.BR jq (1)
or
.B bws
are not installed natively,
.B bwx
falls back to Docker-wrapped equivalents automatically.
.\"
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version number and exit.
.\"
.SS "Common per-command options"
Most subcommands accept the following options before positional arguments:
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-refresh
Bypass the cache and force a fresh API fetch.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log\-level " " \fILEVEL\fR
Override the logging verbosity for this invocation.
Valid levels:
.BR error ", " warn ", " info ", " debug ", " trace ", " diag .
.\"
.SH COMMANDS
.\"
.SS "secret family"
Commands for querying and mutating individual secrets.
Every command that accepts a
.I SECRET
argument resolves it by key name or UUID.
Every command that accepts an optional
.I PROJECT
argument defaults to the value of
.BR BWX_DEFAULT_PROJECT .
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx secret list " "[--refresh] [PROJECT]"
List all secrets in a project as compact JSON.
Pipe through
.BR jq (1)
to pretty-print.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx secret show " "SECRET [PROJECT]"
Print the full JSON metadata for a single secret, including key, value,
note, id, and timestamps.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx secret get " "[--refresh] PROPERTY SECRET [PROJECT]"
Get a single property of a secret.
.I PROPERTY
is one of:
.BR value ,
.BR note ,
.BR id ,
.BR key ,
.BR name ,
.BR filename ,
.BR tags ,
.BR expires ,
.BR provider ,
.BR mode .
The
.B tags
property prints one tag per line.
See
.B STRUCTURED NOTE METADATA
for details on note-derived properties.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx secret set " "[--from-file FILE] [--force] PROPERTY SECRET [VALUE] [PROJECT]"
Set a property of a secret.
Settable properties:
.BR value ,
.BR note ,
.BR key ,
.BR filename ,
.BR mode .
.I VALUE
is required unless
.B \-\-from\-file
or
.B \-\-force
is given.
Use
.B \-\-from\-file
to read the new value from a file (useful for multi-line content).
Use
.B \-\-force
to allow setting an empty value.
The
.B mode
property takes an octal file mode (for example,
.BR 0644 )
and is honored by
.BR "bwx import" .
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx secret ls " "[--refresh] [PROJECT]"
Print secret key names only, one per line, sorted.
A compact alternative to
.BR "bwx secret list" .
.\"
.TP
\fBbwx secret create\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fIKEY\fR [\fIVALUE\fR] [\fIPROJECT\fR]
Create a new secret.
The value can be given as a positional argument or read from a file with
.BR \-\-from\-file .
Options:
.RS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-description " " \fIDESC\fR
Set the
.B note:
field in the structured note.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-note " " \fINOTE\fR
Deprecated alias for
.BR \-\-description .
.TP
.B \-\-note\-from\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Read the description from a file (supports multi-line content).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Set the
.B file:
field in the structured note (deployment filename).
.TP
.B \-\-from\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Read the secret value from a file.
.TP
.B \-\-release\-tag " " \fITAG\fR
Add a
.B release\-tag:
entry to the note.
Repeatable.
.RE
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx secret clone " "SECRET [VALUE] [PROJECT]"
Deep-copy a secret and increment the version suffix.
The source secret name must end in
.B _vN
(for example,
.BR api_key_v1 ).
The clone is created as
.BR _v(N+1) .
All note metadata is preserved except release tags, which are stripped.
An optional new
.I VALUE
replaces the original.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx secret delete " "SECRET [PROJECT]"
Delete a secret by name or UUID.
.\"
.SS "project family"
Commands for querying Bitwarden Secrets Manager projects.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx project list " "[--refresh]"
List all projects as compact JSON.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx project show " "[PROJECT]"
Print the full JSON metadata for a single project.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx project id " "[PROJECT]"
Resolve a project name to its UUID.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx project name " "[PROJECT]"
Resolve a project UUID to its human-readable name.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx project ls " "[--refresh]"
Print project names only, one per line, sorted.
.\"
.TP
.B bwx project default id
Print the UUID of the default project (resolved from
.BR BWX_DEFAULT_PROJECT ).
.\"
.TP
.B bwx project default name
Print the name of the default project.
.\"
.SS "config family"
Commands for storing credentials outside the environment.
See
.B CREDENTIAL RESOLUTION
for precedence and permission rules.
.\"
.TP
.B "bwx config list"
Summarize every recognized configuration entry: the environment
variable it populates, its sensitivity class, whether a file is
stored, that file's mode, and which source currently takes effect.
Values are never printed.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx config path " "[NAME]"
Print the configuration directory, or one entry's full file path when
.I NAME
is given.
Nothing is created and the path need not exist yet.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx config get " NAME
Print a stored configuration value.
Reports the stored value, not the effective one: an environment
variable of the same purpose overrides the file at run time but is not
consulted here.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx config set " "NAME [VALUE]"
Store a configuration value.
When
.I VALUE
is omitted it is read from standard input.
Prefer the piped form for credentials: a value passed as an argument
is visible in the process table and in shell history, a value piped in
is not.
.\"
.SS "tag family"
Commands for managing release tags.
Release tags are stored as
.B release\-tag:
lines in each secret's note field.
They bind secrets to specific deployment releases.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx tag list " "[--refresh] [PROJECT]"
List all distinct release tags across all secrets in a project, one per
line, sorted.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx tag secrets " "[--refresh] [TAG] [PROJECT]"
List secrets grouped by release tag.
If
.I TAG
is specified, only secrets with that tag are shown.
Output format is
.BR "TAG: secret1 secret2 ..." .
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx tag add " "SECRET TAG [PROJECT]"
Add a release tag to a single secret.
Idempotent; if the tag already exists, the note is unchanged.
.\"
.TP
.BI "bwx tag remove " "SECRET TAG [PROJECT]"
Remove a release tag from a single secret.
.\"
.TP
\fBbwx tag project\fR [\fB\-p\fR \fIPROJECT\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fITAG\fR]... [\fB\-R\fR] \fITAG\fR [\fISECRETS\fR...]
Add a release tag to multiple secrets in bulk.
Without explicit
.I SECRETS
or
.BR \-\-select\-tag ,
tags all secrets in the project.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-project " " \fIPROJECT\fR
Project name or UUID.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-select\-tag " " \fITAG\fR
Select secrets that already have this tag.
Repeatable.
Supplements any positional
.IR SECRETS .
.RE
.\"
.TP
\fBbwx tag unproject\fR [\fB\-p\fR \fIPROJECT\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fITAG\fR]... [\fB\-R\fR] \fITAG\fR [\fISECRETS\fR...]
Remove a release tag from multiple secrets in bulk.
Without explicit
.I SECRETS
or
.BR \-\-select\-tag ,
removes the tag from all secrets in the project that have it.
Options are the same as
.BR "bwx tag project" .
.\"
.SS "import"
.TP
\fBbwx import\fR [\fB\-m\fR \fIMODE\fR] [\fB\-\-force\-mode\fR \fIMODE\fR] \fITAG\fR \fIOUTPUT_DIR\fR [\fIPROJECT\fR]
Export all secrets tagged with
.I TAG
from a project into
.IR OUTPUT_DIR .
Each secret with a matching
.B release\-tag:
note entry is written as a file named by its
.B file:
property.
Values are stored in
.IB OUTPUT_DIR /.by\-uuid/ id
with symlinks from the deployment filenames.
.IP
Raw secret JSON is stored in
.IB OUTPUT_DIR /.raw/ id
using the secret UUID as the filename.
.IB OUTPUT_DIR /.raw/MANIFEST
maps each UUID back to the original secret key.
.IP
The special tag
.B all
exports every secret regardless of tagging.
.IP
Exported files default to mode
.B 0600
and their containing directories are always
.BR 0700 .
Per-file precedence, most specific first:
.BR \-\-force\-mode ,
the secret's own
.B mode:
note field,
.B \-\-mode
(or
.BR BWX_IMPORT_FILE_MODE ),
then
.BR 0600 .
.RS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " \fIMODE\fR
Deferential octal mode (for example,
.BR 0644 ),
applied only to secrets whose note does not set
.BR mode: .
.TP
.BR \-\-force\-mode " " \fIMODE\fR
Assertive octal mode applied to every exported file, overriding any
per-secret
.B mode:
field.
.RE
.\"
.SS "check"
.TP
\fBbwx check expiry\fR [\fB\-\-exit\-on\-expiring\fR] [\fB\-\-warn\-days\fR \fIDAYS\fR] [\fIPROJECT\fR]
Check for secrets with upcoming or past expiration dates.
Reads the
.B expires:
field from each secret's note.
Secrets without an
.B expires:
field are silently skipped.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-exit\-on\-expiring
Exit with status 1 if any expired or soon-expiring secrets are found.
Useful as a pre-release gate.
.TP
.BR \-\-warn\-days " " \fIDAYS\fR
Warning window in days.
Default: 14.
.RE
.\"
.SS "note"
.TP
\fBbwx note validate\fR [\fB\-\-provider\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-q\fR] \fISECRET\fR [\fIPROJECT\fR]
Validate a secret's note fields without performing rotation.
Core fields are checked for format:
.B file:
must be a safe relative filename,
.B expires:
must be
.BR YYYY\-MM\-DD ,
.B mode:
must be an octal file mode, and
.B provider:
and
.B release\-tag:
must match
.BR [A\-Za\-z0\-9._\-] .
When a provider is set (or supplied with
.BR \-\-provider ),
each provider config field is checked against its declared type and
required fields must be present.
Credential references are checked for syntax only; no Bitwarden
lookups, file reads, or environment access occur.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-\-provider " " \fINAME\fR
Override or supply the provider used for config-field validation.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the success message.
.RE
.\"
.SS "rotate"
.TP
\fBbwx rotate\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] \fISECRET\fR [\fIPROJECT\fR]
.TQ
\fBbwx rotate \-\-all\fR [\fIPROJECT\fR]
Rotate a time-limited secret using its provider driver.
The provider is determined by the
.B provider:
field in the secret's note.
When no provider is set, the generic
.B prompt
driver asks the operator to paste a new value.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-all
Rotate all secrets that have an
.B expires:
field.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be done without making changes.
.RE
.\"
.SS "provider"
.TP
.BI "bwx provider info " NAME
Print the note fields a rotation provider reads, with each field's
type and default.
Fields with no default are marked
.BR (required) .
The provider is classified as
.B automated
or
.BR interactive .
Provider source is parsed statically; no provider code runs.
.TP
.B bwx provider info \-\-list
Print the names of all available providers, one per line.
.\"
.SS "raw"
.TP
.BI "bwx raw " "[bws-args...]"
Pass-through to the upstream
.BR bws (1)
binary (or Docker-wrapped equivalent).
All arguments are forwarded without modification.
.\"
.SS "completion"
.TP
.B bwx completion bash
Print bash completion definitions to stdout.
.TP
.B bwx completion zsh
Print zsh completion definitions to stdout.
.IP
Setup:
.RS
.nf
# Bash (add to ~/.bashrc)
eval "$(bwx completion bash)"

# Zsh (add to ~/.zshrc)
eval "$(bwx completion zsh)"
.fi
.RE
.\"
.SH STRUCTURED NOTE METADATA
.B bwx
stores structured metadata in the Bitwarden Secrets Manager note field
using a line-oriented
.IB key ": " value
format.
.SS Properties
.TP
.B file:
Maps the secret to a deployment filename.
Used by
.B bwx import
to write the secret value to disk.
Single-value.
.TP
.B note:
Human-readable description of the secret's purpose.
Single-value.
.TP
.B expires:
Expiration date in ISO 8601 format (e.g.,
.BR 2026-09-20 ).
Used by
.B bwx check expiry
to detect upcoming expirations.
Single-value.
.TP
.B provider:
Rotation provider driver name (e.g.,
.BR tailscale-oauth ,
.BR github-pat ).
Used by
.B bwx rotate
to determine how to generate a new credential.
Falls back to
.B prompt
if not set.
Single-value.
.TP
.B mode:
Octal file mode (for example,
.BR 0644 )
applied to the exported file by
.BR "bwx import" .
Overrides the
.B \-\-mode
default but yields to
.BR \-\-force\-mode .
Single-value.
.TP
.B release\-tag:
Release identifier binding the secret to a specific deployment.
Multi-value; each tag is a separate line.
Managed by
.B bwx tag add
and
.BR "bwx tag remove" .
.\"
.SS "Field naming"
The unhyphenated names above
.RB ( file ,
.BR note ,
.BR expires ,
.BR provider ,
.BR mode )
and
.B release\-tag
are reserved for the framework.
Every provider config field and custom metadata field must contain at
least one hyphen, prefixed with the provider's domain (for example,
.BR grafana\-url ,
.BR cert\-days ,
.BR aws\-iam\-username ).
.B bwx note validate
enforces this convention.
.\"
.SS "Example note"
.nf
file: mosquitto-password
note: MQTT broker authentication credential
expires: 2026-09-20
mode: 0640
provider: mqtt-password
release-tag: 2026.06.01.01
release-tag: 2026.06.24.01
.fi
.\"
.SH ROTATION PROVIDERS
Providers live in
.I lib/providers/<name>
and export a function
.BI bwx-provider- name ().
Each provider sets
.BR PROVIDER_VALUE ,
.BR PROVIDER_EXPIRES ,
and
.B PROVIDER_NOTE
before returning.
Provider config is read from hyphenated fields in the secret's note;
.B bwx provider info
prints the fields a given provider accepts.
.PP
Fields marked
.I credential
below accept any of four reference forms:
.BI project : secret
(read from another Bitwarden secret),
.BI ./ path
(a file under
.BR $BWX_SECRETS_DIR ),
.BI @env: VAR
(an environment variable), or a literal value.
Several providers also fall back to files in
.B $BWX_SECRETS_DIR
named for the field when the note omits it.
.\"
.SS "Automated providers"
These run without operator input.
.\"
.TP
.B aws-iam
Create a new AWS IAM access key and deactivate the old one via the
.BR aws (1)
CLI (or its Docker-wrapped equivalent).
Fields:
.B aws\-iam\-username
(default: the caller's own user),
.B aws\-access\-key\-id
and
.B aws\-secret\-access\-key
.RI ( credential ;
absent both, the native AWS credential chain is used), and
.B aws\-region
(default:
.BR us\-east\-1 ).
.\"
.TP
.B bitwarden-api-key
Create a new access token for a Bitwarden machine account via the
Bitwarden API.
Fields:
.B bitwarden\-org\-id
and
.B bitwarden\-machine\-account\-id
.RI ( credential ).
.\"
.TP
.B docker-registry
Create a new Docker Hub personal access token via the Hub API.
Fields:
.B docker\-token\-label
(default:
.BR bwx\-rotated ),
.B docker\-hub\-username
and
.B docker\-hub\-password
.RI ( credential ).
.\"
.TP
.B grafana-service-account
Create a new token for a Grafana service account via the HTTP API.
Fields:
.B grafana\-url
(default:
.BR http://localhost:3000 ),
.B grafana\-sa\-id
(required),
.B grafana\-token\-name
(default:
.BR bwx\-rotated ),
.B grafana\-admin\-user
(default:
.BR admin ;
.IR credential ),
and
.B grafana\-admin\-password
(required;
.IR credential ).
.\"
.TP
.B mqtt-password
Generate a random alphanumeric password for an MQTT broker.
The consuming broker's password file must be updated separately.
No config fields.
.\"
.TP
.B openssl-selfsigned
Generate a self-signed TLS certificate and private key via
.BR openssl (1)
(or its Docker-wrapped equivalent).
Give the certificate and the key separate secrets, each with
.B provider: openssl-selfsigned
and a distinct
.BR cert\-role .
Fields:
.B cert\-role
.RB ( cert ,
the default, or
.BR key ),
.B cert\-cn
(default:
.BR bwx\-selfsigned ),
and
.B cert\-days
(default: 365; minimum: 1).
.\"
.TP
.B password-generate
Generate a cryptographically random password from
.IR /dev/urandom .
Fields:
.B password\-length
(8\(en256; default: 32) and
.B password\-charset
.RB ( alphanumeric
or
.BR alphanumeric+symbols ,
the default).
.\"
.TP
.B tailscale-oauth
Create a tagged Tailscale pre-auth key via OAuth client credentials.
Fields:
.B tailscale\-oauth\-client\-id
and
.B tailscale\-oauth\-client\-secret
.RI ( credential ).
Creates a key with 90-day expiry.
.\"
.SS "Interactive providers"
These guide the operator through a paste-and-validate flow on the
terminal.
.\"
.TP
.B anthropic-api-key
Paste an Anthropic API key.
Validates the
.B sk-ant-
prefix.
.\"
.TP
.B github-pat
Paste a GitHub Personal Access Token.
Validates token format
.RB ( ghp_ *
or
.BR github_pat_ *).
Default: 365-day expiry.
.\"
.TP
.B letsencrypt-manual
Paste a PEM-encoded Let's Encrypt certificate.
Validates PEM format and sets a fixed 90-day expiry matching the
certificate lifetime.
.\"
.TP
.B tailscale-manual
Paste a key from the Tailscale admin console.
Used for untagged keys, which OAuth clients cannot create.
Supports custom expiry entry.
.\"
.TP
.B prompt
Generic operator-prompted value paste.
Default fallback when no
.B provider:
field is set.
Asks for a new value and expiry in days (default: 90).
.\"
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BWS_ACCESS_TOKEN
(Required.)
Bitwarden Secrets Manager machine-account access token.
Validated on first API call; the result is cached for
.B BWX_VALIDATE_ACCESS_TTL_SECONDS
seconds.
Falls back to a file when unset; see
.BR "CREDENTIAL RESOLUTION" .
.TP
.B BWX_DEFAULT_PROJECT
Default project name for all commands.
When set, the
.RI [ PROJECT ]
argument can be omitted from every subcommand.
Falls back to a file when unset; see
.BR "CREDENTIAL RESOLUTION" .
.TP
.B BWS_SERVER_BASE_URL
Bitwarden server URL.
Default:
.BR https://vault.bitwarden.com .
Override for self-hosted instances.
.TP
.B BWX_SECRET_LIST_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS
TTL in seconds for secret-list and project-list file caches.
Default: 300 (5 minutes).
Set to 0 to disable file caching.
.TP
.B BWX_VALIDATE_ACCESS_TTL_SECONDS
TTL in seconds for caching access-token validation results.
Default: 300.
.TP
.B BWX_CACHE_DIR
Override the cache directory location.
Default:
.BR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/bwx
(or
.BR $HOME/.cache/bwx ).
.TP
.B BWX_CONFIG_DIR
Override the configuration directory location.
Default:
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bwx
(or
.BR $HOME/.config/bwx ).
.TP
.B BWX_SECRETS_DIR
Directory searched by rotation providers for credential files and
accepted as the root for
.BI ./ path
credential references.
Default:
.BR .secrets .
.TP
.B BWX_IMPORT_FILE_MODE
Default octal mode for files written by
.BR "bwx import" ,
equivalent to passing
.BR \-\-mode .
Yields to a secret's own
.B mode:
field and to
.BR \-\-force\-mode .
.TP
.B BWX_JQ_IMAGE
Docker image for
.BR jq (1)
when not natively installed.
Default:
.BR ghcr.io/jqlang/jq:1.8.2 .
.TP
.B BWX_BWS_IMAGE
Docker image for
.B bws
when not natively installed.
Default:
.BR bitwarden/bws:latest .
.TP
.B BWX_CURL_IMAGE
Docker image for
.BR curl (1)
when not natively installed.
Default:
.BR curlimages/curl .
.TP
.B BWX_OPENSSL_IMAGE
Docker image for
.BR openssl (1)
when not natively installed.
Default:
.BR alpine/openssl .
.TP
.B BWX_AWS_IMAGE
Docker image for the
.B aws
CLI when not natively installed.
Default:
.BR amazon/aws\-cli .
.TP
.B BWS_CONFIG_FILE
Path to a
.B bws
config file.
If unset, a temporary config is generated from
.BR BWS_SERVER_BASE_URL .
.TP
.B DEBUG
Retained for compatibility; it does not enable shell xtrace.
Secret-handling commands deliberately avoid xtrace so secret values are
never written to the trace stream.
For verbose diagnostics set
.B LOG_LEVEL
to
.BR debug " or " trace .
.TP
.B LOG_LEVEL
Logging verbosity.
Default:
.BR info .
Available levels:
.BR error ", " warn ", " info ", " debug ", " trace ", " diag .
.\"
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
General error.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Configuration error (missing or invalid environment variables).
.TP
.B 4
Resource not found (secret, project, or provider does not exist).
.TP
.B 5
Fatal error (unrecoverable).
.\"
.SH CACHING
.B bwx
caches Bitwarden API responses in two layers to reduce API calls.
.\"
.SS "Layer 1: environment variables"
Secret lists are stored in shell variables named
.BI BWS_PROJECT_SECRET_LIST_ PROJECT
(project name uppercased, non-alphanumeric characters replaced with
underscores).
This cache lives for the duration of the shell session.
.\"
.SS "Layer 2: file cache"
JSON responses are persisted to
.B $BWX_CACHE_DIR
(default:
.BR $HOME/.cache/bwx/ ).
Files are keyed by a SHA-256 hash of the server URL, access token, and
project identifier.
Cache files are created with mode
.B 0600
inside a directory with mode
.BR 0700 .
.\"
.SS "TTL"
Both cache layers use the same TTL, controlled by
.B BWX_SECRET_LIST_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS
(default: 300 seconds).
.\"
.SS "Forced refresh"
Pass
.B \-\-refresh
(or
.BR \-R )
to any
.B list
command to bypass both cache layers.
Mutating commands automatically refresh the cache after a successful
update.
.\"
.SH CREDENTIAL RESOLUTION
.B BWS_ACCESS_TOKEN
and
.B BWX_DEFAULT_PROJECT
resolve from the environment first, then from a file in the
configuration directory named for the value it holds
.RB ( bws\-access\-token
and
.BR bwx\-default\-project ).
An exported variable always wins.
.PP
The file layer exists because a non-interactive shell returns from
.I ~/.bashrc
before reaching anything below the standard
.B "case $\- in *i*) ;; *) return;; esac"
guard.
A token exported further down that file is therefore invisible to
.BR cron ,
.BR "ssh host command" ,
and
.BR systemd ,
and the failure is silent because interactive logins keep working.
A file under
.I $HOME
is visible to all of them, and survives redeployment of any working
tree.
.PP
Entries are classified
.B secret
or
.BR plain .
A
.B secret
file readable by group or others is refused on read, in the same
spirit as
.BR ssh (1)
rejecting a world-readable private key.
The check runs only when the file is actually read: when the
environment already supplies the value, the file is never opened.
Use
.B "bwx config set"
to write these files with the correct mode.
.\"
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $BWX_CACHE_DIR/
File-based cache for API responses.
.TP
.I $BWX_CONFIG_DIR/bws\-access\-token
Stored access token, mode
.BR 0600 .
.TP
.I $BWX_CONFIG_DIR/bwx\-default\-project
Stored default project identifier.
.TP
.I $BWX_SECRETS_DIR/
Directory for rotation provider credential files (default:
.BR .secrets ).
.TP
.I OUTPUT_DIR/.by\-uuid/
Secret values written by
.BR "bwx import" ,
keyed by UUID; the deployment filenames are symlinks into it.
.TP
.I OUTPUT_DIR/.raw/
Raw secret JSON written by
.BR "bwx import" ,
plus a
.I MANIFEST
mapping each UUID to its secret key.
.\"
.SH EXAMPLES
Store the access token for unattended callers without exposing it in
the process table:
.PP
.nf
$ pbpaste | bwx config set bws\-access\-token
$ bwx config list
.fi
.PP
List all secret names in the default project:
.PP
.nf
$ bwx secret ls
api_key_v1
db_password_v3
mqtt_broker_password_v1
.fi
.PP
Get the value of a secret:
.PP
.nf
$ bwx secret get value mqtt_broker_password_v1
s3cret
.fi
.PP
Create a secret with metadata:
.PP
.nf
$ bwx secret create mqtt_broker_password_v1 "s3cret" \e
    --file mosquitto-password \e
    --description "MQTT broker authentication" \e
    --release-tag 2026.06.24.01
.fi
.PP
Tag all secrets in a project for a release:
.PP
.nf
$ bwx tag project 2026.06.24.01
.fi
.PP
Export tagged secrets to a directory, with group-readable files unless
a secret's note says otherwise:
.PP
.nf
$ bwx import --mode 0640 2026.06.24.01 .secrets
.fi
.PP
Check for expiring secrets (CI gate):
.PP
.nf
$ bwx check expiry --exit-on-expiring --warn-days 30
.fi
.PP
See which note fields a provider reads, then validate a secret's note
before rotating it:
.PP
.nf
$ bwx provider info grafana-service-account
$ bwx note validate grafana_sa_token_v1
.fi
.PP
Rotate a secret using its provider:
.PP
.nf
$ bwx rotate tailscale_sidecar_authkey_v1
.fi
.PP
Rotate all expiring secrets (dry run):
.PP
.nf
$ bwx rotate --all --dry-run
.fi
.PP
Pass-through to upstream bws:
.PP
.nf
$ bwx raw secret get aaaa-bbbb-cccc-dddd --output json
.fi
.\"
